{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":""The Way You Move" is a song recorded by Big Boi of the American hip hop duo OutKast, released by LaFace Records.","title":"The Way You Move"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The song features OutKast mentor Sleepy Brown on guest vocals.","title":"The Way You Move"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Along with "Hey Ya!","title":"The Way You Move"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":"", recorded by OutKast's other member André 3000, "The Way You Move" is one of the two lead singles from "Speakerboxxx/The Love Below", OutKast's double album project which includes a solo album from each member.","title":"The Way You Move"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lecrae is an American Christian hip hop artist.","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" His career began in 2004 when he and Ben Washer co-founded the record label Reach Records.","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 2007 his first album, "Real Talk" (2005)"," received a nomination at the Stellar Awards and his second album, "After the Music Stops" (2007), was nominated at the GMA Dove Awards.","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The following year Lecrae's third album, "Rebel", became the first Christian hip hop album to chart at number one on the U.S. "Billboard" Gospel Albums Chart.","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In 2011 his fourth album, "Rehab" (2010), received a Grammy nomination for Best Rock Gospel Album.","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" That year Lecrae began achieving mainstream success and recognition after he collaborated with DJ Statik Selektah on the song "Live & Let Live" and performed at the 2011 BET Hip Hop Awards Cypher.","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The following year he garnered two GMA Dove awards: Rap/Hip Hop Album of the Year for "" (2011) and Rap/Hip Hop Recorded Song of the Year for "Hallelujah" (2011).","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" He also released the mixtape "Church Clothes" and the studio album "Gravity", the latter of which of has been called the most important album in Christian hip hop history by Rapzilla and "Atlanta Daily World".","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: noanswer
